__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
# Any .env variant - NOT just ".env". A `cp .env .env.bak-151721`
# safety copy made before editing was matched by none of these rules,
# got swept up by `git add -A`, and was pushed to GitHub with every
# secret in it (2026-09-24 - the bot token was stolen and used within
# hours). The negation keeps the committed template tracked.
.env.*
!.env.dist
*.log
.venv/
venv/
reminders.json
.aussies_cache/
usage_stats.json
.releases_cache/
.knowledge_cache/
.bonuses_cache/
orna_model_compare.json
# .qa_cache/ is deliberately COMMITTED, unlike every other cache here. It is the
# raw r/OrnaRPG crawl - 800 threads' comments - and it is the one artefact that
# is expensive to reproduce: an hour of rate-limited fetching that took three
# runs and four 429 backoffs to complete. Keeping it means orna_scrape_qa.py can
# resume or extend from any checkout without re-fetching, and that a lost working
# copy costs nothing. The other caches stay ignored because they refetch in
# seconds (.aussies_cache) or have a committed fallback (.knowledge_cache ->
# orna_knowledge.txt).
amities.json
nicknames.json
codex.sqlite3
codex.sqlite3-shm
codex.sqlite3-wal
codex.sqlite3.tmp
